  "user_request_original": "Execute TMM optimization for 12-layer Ta2O5/SiO2 alternating stack on fused silica substrate at 0 deg incidence unpolarized. Layer sequence: Ta2O5|SiO2|Ta2O5|SiO2|Ta2O5|SiO2|Ta2O5|SiO2|Ta2O5|SiO2|Ta2O5|SiO2 (12 finite layers). Thickness bounds: [10,400]nm for all layers. Initialize with uniform random sampling across bounds. Optimize to maximize average transmittance in 420-700nm band while minimizing average transmittance in 355-365nm and 1030-1080nm bands and minimizing transmittance at 355nm. Simulation grid: 300-1200nm with 1nm resolution. Use gradient_thickness optimizer with 4 independent runs from different random seeds. Canonical user controls: incidence angles 0 degrees. polarization unpolarized. wavelength intervals 355-355 nm, 355-365 nm, 420-700 nm, 1030-1080 nm. soft objectives: high average transmittance in 420-700 nm; low average transmittance at 355 nm; low average transmittance in 355-365 nm; low average transmittance in 1030-1080 nm. behaviors to suppress or avoid: high transmittance at 355 nm; high transmittance in 355-365 nm; high transmittance in 1030-1080 nm; high loss in 420-700 nm. manufacturing constraints: maximum 36 layers; layer thickness range 20-350 nm.",
